   - Visible in listings: shown in category listings and search. Has no effect on collections.
   - Available for purchase: when off, customers can see the product but cannot buy it.
 - Availability diagnostics explain why a product is not purchasable.
+- Age-restricted products: a per-product flag. The product stays visible to everyone; buying it needs a customer who meets the store minimum age.
 - Categories form a tree. Collections are curated product groups. Attributes belong to one of three families: product, model or customer.
   - Input types: dropdown, multiselect, file, reference, single reference, plain text, rich text, numeric, boolean, date, date-time, swatch.
 - Bulk publish to a channel is a wizard with four steps: select, defaults, review, confirm. It can set the visibility switches, prices and stock in one go.
@@ -58,6 +59,7 @@ Glossary: the root `CONTEXT.md` is canonical (Model, Model type, Model type grou
 
 ## Customers and pricing
 - Customers have a profile, addresses, a note, an active or inactive status and an order history. Their KPIs are shown per channel.
+- Age verification: staff see a yes or no eligibility flag for age-restricted products. Only a superuser can set the customer's date of birth, and other staff do not see it.
 - Customer types (for example B2B or Wholesale) add type-specific attributes to customers. The customer list has a tab per type.
 - Discounts:
   - Catalogue promotions target products, categories, collections or variants. Order promotions target the order subtotal or total.
@@ -83,6 +85,7 @@ Glossary: the root `CONTEXT.md` is canonical (Model, Model type, Model type grou
 - Staff invite: email, name and permission groups (default "Full Access" when the inviter may grant it). The invitee sets a password from a link. A pending invite is an active account that has never signed in.
 - Staff cannot change their own status. Changing an email needs MANAGE_STAFF, even for one's own account. A permission group is read-only to a viewer who lacks any of its permissions.
 - Site settings: store details, the password-login mode (all, customers only, off) and address-field preservation.
+- Age restriction (site settings): the minimum age for age-restricted products (1 to 120) and the store time zone that sets the age check day.
 - Notifications: staff emails (store mail server), order-alert recipients and customer emails (handled by an app). Refund and return reasons each come from a chosen model type.
 
 ## Home, onboarding, search, announcements
